*(
    title: Microscopy and Cell Theory
    description: The instruments that made cells visible, and the three claims that hardened into a theory.
    tags: microscopy, cell theory, magnification, resolution, module 1, biology
    lesson
)

// Abbe's diffraction limit, d = lambda / (2 NA), with lambda = 550 nm (green,
// the middle of the visible band). At the best oil-immersion NA of 1.4 this is
// 550 / 2.8 = 196 nm, which is the 0.2 um quoted as the light microscope's floor.
@let(
    abbe floor: 196
)

@include(src: ../preface.part.chalk)

